WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.435
-The Oscars were last night,

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.871
and here with a recap is one
of our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.340
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.676
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:14.313
-You guys! What?!

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:16.415
The Oscars were crazy!

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:20.887
Okay, first of all,
everyone looked too beautiful.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:24.056
Danai Gurira's dress
was like, what?!

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:27.794
Then Kacey Musgraves' dress
was like, what?!

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.897
And then Regina King's leg
was like, what?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.699
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.703
Then people were like, "You have
to see Billy Porter's tuxedo."

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.971
And I was like, "What?"

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:42.075
Then I saw the whole thing!
It was like, what?!

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.144
Aaah! Aaah!

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.481
Then I saw Paul Rudd

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:53.286
and was like, "What...
is Paul Rudd's son doing here?"

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.821
Then someone was like,
"That's Paul Rudd."

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:59.492
And I was like, "Which one
of his parents is black?

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.995
Because it has not cracked."

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:05.364
Then...

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.834
Then the night started,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.336
and everyone was like,
"Who is gonna win?"

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.238
And every black person I know
was like,

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.874
"Who cares, as long
as it's not 'Green Book.'"

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.475
[ Laughter ]
-Whoo!

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:19.712
-Then -- Whoo right back at ya.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:24.217
Then right off the bat,
"Black Panther" won two Oscars!

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.152
And I was like, "What, what?!"

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.754
Yay!

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:30.489
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:35.027
And then Bradley Cooper
and Lady Gaga sang a duet.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:42.000
And I was like ♪ Whaaaaaat ♪

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.869
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.672
Then "Green Book" --

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.774
Yeah, you can clap extra
'cause it was so great.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:52.011
Then "Green Book"
won Best Screenplay.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:56.549
But the real star was
Samuel L. Jackson's face.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.417
'Cause he opened up
that envelope,

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.587
and his face was like, "What?"

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.521
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.555
Look at him!

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.390
[ Applause ]

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.126
I haven't seen his face
look like that

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.663
since there were a bunch
of snakes on his plane.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.866
Now, if you think
that face was rude,

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.533
let me give you
a little backstory.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:16.636
A million years ago,
Samuel L. Jackson

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.704
was in a Spike Lee movie
called "Do the Right Thing,"

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.773
which is one of the best movies
of all time

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.208
and wasn't even nominated.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.276
The winner that year
was "Driving Miss Daisy."

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:25.811
Fast-forward to today,

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.915
when another Spike Lee movie
lost to "Driving Miss Daisy 2."

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.217
This time, the white one drives!

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.019
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.155
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:43.362
Then Alfonso Cuarón won
Best Director for "Roma"!

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:46.165
And I was like, "What?!"

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.300
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.937
Then I read that it was
the fifth time in six years

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:54.139
a Mexican director
won Best Director.

00:02:54.139 --> 00:02:56.642
And I was like, "Qué?"

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.979
Shoot.
Five Oscars.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.349
You better put a door in that
border wall for filmmakers.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.583
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.686
Trying to see some movies.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.621
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.323
Aah!

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:14.194
Then Olivia Colman
won Best Actress,

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.828
and she was like
[British accent] "What?

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.763
I thought Glenn Close
was going to win."

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:20.499
[ Normal voice ] And Glenn Close
was like, "Bitch, so did I!"

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.735
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:26.205
"Why do you think I came
dressed as an Oscar?"

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:27.974
Whoo!
[ Audience cheers ]

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.442
Yeah! [ Laughs ]

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.077
That was so call and response.

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:33.713
Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.914
-Y'all stupid.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.850
And I was rooting
for Glenn Close,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:42.121
because we feel the same way
about Billy Porter's outfit.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.457
Check out what she did when
she saw it on the red carpet.

00:03:45.457 --> 00:03:48.294
-The children are serving us
with their looks

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.229
on the red carpet.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.732
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.737
-Now, I don't know what happened
to her in that moment,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.739
but I think it was better
than winning an Oscar.

00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:03.576
Then "Green Book"
won Best Picture.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:07.547
And I was like, "What?
Oh, no!"

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.415
And I yelled it so loud,
I woke up my husband,

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.250
and he was like,
"What, did someone break in?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.851
What's wrong?"
And I was like, "Worse!"

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:15.021
'Green Book' won Best Picture."

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.489
And that made me really sad.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.792
So I thought about my favorite
thing that happened this week.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.660
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.195
Not that one.

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:25.798
My second favorite thing
that happened this week.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.867
Yay!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:33.373
This has been
"Amber Says ♪ Whaaaat ♪"

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.744
-Give it up for Amber Ruffin,
everybody.

